        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A concrete repair kit is a good buy when its contents match one specific job. Injection kits are the best way for a homeowner to seal a single leaking poured wall crack, and buying the parts separately rarely saves money there.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For slab cracks, broken edges and worn surfaces, the components usually beat the kit on both price and quality. Identify the damage, decide whether it is still moving, and buy the product built for that, not the box with the most dramatic photo.
          </p>
